From: Daniel Borkmann <daniel@iogearbox.net>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 13:52:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] bpf: Treat dentry->d_parent as a trusted pointer

An LSM program that decides a new directory entry in inode_create,
inode_mkdir, inode_symlink, inode_mknod or inode_link receives the
directory as a struct inode and the new entry as a dentry. The
directory's label lives in an xattr that bpf_get_dentry_xattr() reads
from a dentry, and the one the program has for it is dentry->d_parent,
which the verifier treats as an untrusted pointer, so the kfunc refuses
it and the program cannot read the label of the directory it decides
on.

d_parent of a dentry an inode hook receives is stable while the hook
runs, under the parent's inode lock the caller holds, and is never NULL,
since the root's points to itself. Add it beside d_inode as trusted or
null, which keeps a program checking it before use.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Borkmann <daniel@iogearbox.net>
[ spin-stack/machine: from shirudo's testing/kernel/patches, at
  versions.yaml's shirudo pin. ]
---
 kernel/bpf/verifier.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/kernel/bpf/verifier.c b/kernel/bpf/verifier.c
index 26ab4b83b..12066fbc3 100644
--- a/kernel/bpf/verifier.c
+++ b/kernel/bpf/verifier.c
@@ -6616,6 +6616,7 @@ BTF_TYPE_SAFE_TRUSTED(struct scx_sub_detach_args) {
 
 BTF_TYPE_SAFE_TRUSTED_OR_NULL(struct dentry) {
 	struct inode *d_inode;
+	struct dentry *d_parent;
 };
 
 BTF_TYPE_SAFE_TRUSTED_OR_NULL(struct linux_binprm) {
-- 
2.53.0

